Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_rmm: Accept platform-allocated GPTs

RMI_GPT_L1_CREATE returns RMI_ERROR_GLOBAL for platform-allocated PARs.
The current RMM uses statically allocated GPTs, so Linux must accept this
status when initializing metadata. Preserve RMI_ERROR_GPT handling for
tables which have already been created by the host.

---
 drivers/firmware/arm_rmm/rmi.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_rmm/rmi.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_rmm/rmi.c
index 5c4d16f6ea52..de252dab2c45 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_rmm/rmi.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_rmm/rmi.c
@@ -697,8 +697,11 @@ static int rmi_create_gpts(phys_addr_t start, phys_addr_t end)
 		/*
 		 * Make sure the L1 GPT tables are created for the region.
 		 * RMI_ERROR_GPT indicates the L1 table already exists.
+		 * The current RMM returns RMI_ERROR_GLOBAL for static tables.
 		 */
-		if (ret != RMI_SUCCESS && RMI_RETURN_STATUS(ret) != RMI_ERROR_GPT) {
+		if (ret != RMI_SUCCESS &&
+		    RMI_RETURN_STATUS(ret) != RMI_ERROR_GPT &&
+		    RMI_RETURN_STATUS(ret) != RMI_ERROR_GLOBAL) {
 			pr_err("GPT Level1 table missing for %llx\n", start);
 			kfree(sro);
 			return -ENOMEM;
